  "notes": "2026-08-27 re-verification. Every entry cites a page that was fetched and returned HTTP 200 and that states BOTH the before and the after net contents for that product; the `source` field names it. The previous 35 entries were authored from invented data - all 35 evidence_url values 404'd and the size pairs were unsourced - so 18 were removed outright, 17 were corrected against the real Mouse Print* downsizing archive, and 8 documented cases were added. Date convention: `history[1].date` is the publication date of the cited article - the month the smaller package was documented on shelf. `history[0].date` is twelve months earlier, an approximation for 'the size the source says it used to be'. No date here is more precise than that. Every `barcode` is a real GTIN confirmed against the Kroger Products API, USDA FoodData Central and/or Open Food Facts, and identifies the product line the source describes. Where a package has shrunk again since the cited article, the entry still records the documented step; the app's live Kroger and USDA observations show the rest. `current_price` is the shelf price at Kroger Hyde Park, Cincinnati (locationId 01400355) on 2026-08-27.",
